    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Roman numerals and Nashville numbers make chord transposition systematic."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "by-letter",
      "title": "By letter",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "G-D-Em-C up a whole step = A-E-F♯m-D. Move every symbol the same distance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nashville-numbers",
      "title": "Nashville numbers",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "1-5-6m-4 in D = D-A-Bm-G; in G = G-D-Em-C. Session guitarists call changes by number when singers shift key."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "non-diatonic-chords",
      "title": "Non-diatonic chords",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Borrowed ♭VII and secondary dominants transpose with the same interval. Capo: shapes in C with capo 2 sounds in D."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
